List the tasks you requested on your agent swarm, with status and progress. Signed out, shows the read-only demo swarm.

```ts
mcp__Agent_Swarm__get_tasks(args: {
// Filter by task status (unassigned, offered, pending, in_progress, completed, failed).
status?: "draft" | "backlog" | "unassigned" | "offered" | "reviewing" | "pending" | "in_progress" | "paused" | "completed" | "failed" | "cancelled" | "superseded",
// Only return tasks assigned to you.
mineOnly?: boolean,
// Only return unassigned tasks in the pool.
unassigned?: boolean,
// Only return tasks offered to you (awaiting accept/reject).
offeredToMe?: boolean,
// Only return tasks whose dependencies are met.
readyOnly?: boolean,
// Filter by task type (e.g., 'bug', 'feature').
taskType?: string,
// Filter by any matching tag.
tags?: string[],
// Search in task description.
search?: string,
// Filter by schedule ID to find tasks created by a specific schedule.
scheduleId?: string, // format: "uuid"
// Filter by exact logical namespace.
key?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 255
// Filter by namespace subtree.
keyPrefix?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 255
// Include heartbeat/system tasks in results (excluded by default).
includeHeartbeat?: boolean,
// Max tasks to return (default: 25, max: 100).
limit?: integer, // minimum: 1, maximum: 100
// Return the full `task` text instead of a ~300-char `taskPreview`. Default false.
includeFull?: boolean,
// Optional. Which linked swarm to use, by id or URL (see list_swarms). Defaults to your default swarm.
swarm?: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Send a new task to your agent swarm. The swarm's agents pick it up and work on it.

```ts
mcp__Agent_Swarm__send_task(args: {
// The task description to send.
task: string, // minLength: 1
// Task type (e.g., 'bug', 'feature', 'review').
taskType?: string, // maxLength: 50
// Tags for filtering (e.g., ['urgent']).
tags?: string[],
// Priority 0-100 (default: 50).
priority?: integer, // minimum: 0, maximum: 100
// Concrete model override interpreted by the assignee's harness/provider.
model?: string, // minLength: 1
// Portable model tier: 'smol', 'regular', 'smart', or 'ultra'. Resolved by the assignee's harness/provider.
modelTier?: "smol" | "regular" | "smart" | "ultra",
// Optional JSON Schema the assignee's final output must satisfy. store-progress rejects a completion that does not match. Supported keywords: type, required, properties, enum, const, items.
outputSchema?: { [key: string]: any },
// Optional. Which linked swarm to use, by id or URL (see list_swarms). Defaults to your default swarm.
swarm?: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

