Use this when the user researches a company, supplier, or market: registration, filings, legitimacy, competitors, or industry trends. Searches the web and returns links and snippets; results typically include business registries, company filings, regulator warnings, news, and industry sources. Does not look up private individuals. Liner(라이너)

```ts
mcp__Agentic_Search_by_Liner__search_business(args: // Search the public web for general-purpose grounding.
{
// Search query in natural language.
query: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 1000
// Maximum number of results to return.
limit?: integer, // default: 10, minimum: 1, maximum: 50
[key: string]: any,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Use this when the user needs company filings, earnings releases, tax rules, or economic data. Searches the web and returns links and snippets; results typically include securities regulators, exchanges, central banks, tax and statistics agencies, and financial news. Also returns Premium Data tables such as stock prices and earnings estimates when they match the query. Not investment advice. Liner(라이너)

