Render an interactive data table widget with sorting, search, and pagination. Accepts column definitions (key and label) and row data. Column types are inferred automatically from the data. IMPORTANT: preserve array values in row data as JSON arrays (e.g. tags: ["tag1", "tag2"]), do not flatten them to comma-separated strings. The source field is optional: set source.tool to the bare tool name without any connector or namespace prefix (e.g. 'site-explorer-all-backlinks' not 'my-connector:site-explorer-all-backlinks'), and source.params to the arguments you passed, to generate an 'Open in Ahrefs' link.

```ts
mcp__Ahrefs__render_data_table(args: {
columns: Array<
{
// Column key matching row data
key: string,
// Column header label
label: string,
[key: string]: any,
}
>,
pageSize?: integer | null,
rows: any[],
source?:
// The data tool that was called. source.tool must be the bare tool name without any connector or namespace prefix (e.g. 'site-explorer-organic-keywords', not 'my-connector:site-explorer-organic-keywords'). source.params = arguments passed to it. Used to generate 'Open in Ahrefs' link.
 | {
// Tool arguments
params: any,
// MCP tool name
tool: string,
[key: string]: any,
}
 | null
,
title: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Render a scorecard widget showing key metrics as a card grid. Accepts metric cards with labels, raw numeric values, optional unit, optional change indicators, and optional grouping. IMPORTANT: 'value' is a raw number (e.g. 1234567 not '1,234,567' or '1.2M'); the frontend handles all display formatting. Use 'unit' for symbols: '$' for currency, '%' for percentages, 's' for duration in seconds (rendered as e.g. '11m 27s'). Monetary values are in USD cents (not dollars), make sure to divide them by 100 first such that they are displayed in USD. Omit 'value' or pass null for N/A. Change indicators: change.value is a positive number (the percentage amount, e.g. 12.4 for a 12.4% change); change.direction is 'up' or 'down'. When there are more than 4 cards, use the 'group' field to organize them into logical sections (e.g. 'Organic' and 'Paid'). Always include the source field when the data came from an Ahrefs tool call. Set source.tool to the bare tool name without any connector or namespace prefix (e.g. 'site-explorer-metrics' not 'my-connector:site-explorer-metrics'), and source.params to the arguments you passed, to generate an 'Open in Ahrefs' link.

```ts
mcp__Ahrefs__render_scorecard(args: {
cards: Array<
{
// Optional change indicator
change?:
 | {
// up or down
direction: "up" | "down",
// Change percentage
value: number,
[key: string]: any,
}
 | null
,
// Group name for section headers
group?: string | null,
// Metric name
label: string,
// Unit symbol (e.g. '$', '%', 's'). '$' renders as prefix, 's' formats as duration (e.g. 687 -> '11m 27s'), others as suffix.
unit?: string | null,
// Raw numeric value (e.g. 1234567 not '1.2M'). Omit or null for N/A.
value?: number | null,
[key: string]: any,
}
>,
source?:
// The data tool that was called. source.tool must be the bare tool name without any connector or namespace prefix (e.g. 'site-explorer-organic-keywords', not 'my-connector:site-explorer-organic-keywords'). source.params = arguments passed to it. Used to generate 'Open in Ahrefs' link.
 | {
// Tool arguments
params: any,
// MCP tool name
tool: string,
[key: string]: any,
}
 | null
,
title: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Render an interactive time series line chart. Accepts one or more named data series. Supports multi-series with automatic dual Y-axis when 2 series have different units. Features hover tooltip, vertical crosshair, and toggleable legend. IMPORTANT: series names are shown in the chart legend and must be human-readable labels. Convert snake_case identifiers to Title Case (e.g. 'position_1_to_3' becomes 'Position 1 to 3', 'org_traffic' becomes 'Organic Traffic'). Expand abbreviations where possible (e.g. 'ctr' becomes 'CTR', 'org' becomes 'Organic', 'avg' becomes 'Average'). Never pass an empty string as a series name; use a descriptive label like 'Other' or 'Not Set' instead. The source field is optional: set source.tool to the bare tool name without any connector or namespace prefix (e.g. 'brand-radar-sov-history' not 'my-connector:brand-radar-sov-history'), and source.params to the arguments you passed, to generate an 'Open in Ahrefs' link. Unit labels appear next to values in tooltips: only set unit for currencies ('$') or percentages ('%'). Omit unit for all other metrics. Monetary values are in USD cents (not dollars), make sure to divide them by 100 first such that they are displayed in USD.

```ts
mcp__Ahrefs__render_time_series_chart(args: {
series: Array<
{
// Array of date/value points
data: Array<
{
// Date in YYYY-MM-DD format
date: string,
// Numeric value
value: number,
[key: string]: any,
}
>,
// Series name for the legend
name: string,
// Unit symbol displayed next to values in tooltips. Only set for currencies or percentages (e.g. '$', '%'). Omit for everything else (clicks, impressions, position, traffic, etc.). Never pass raw identifiers like 'usd_cents'.
unit?: string | null,
[key: string]: any,
}
>,
source?:
// The data tool that was called. source.tool must be the bare tool name without any connector or namespace prefix (e.g. 'site-explorer-organic-keywords', not 'my-connector:site-explorer-organic-keywords'). source.params = arguments passed to it. Used to generate 'Open in Ahrefs' link.
 | {
// Tool arguments
params: any,
// MCP tool name
tool: string,
[key: string]: any,
}
 | null
,
title: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

