Deletes a page from an interface, given its pageId.
Standalone forms, and pages that have no published version yet, are removed immediately. A
page that has its own published version is instead staged for removal in the working draft,
staying visible to end users until the interface is published.
An immediate removal cannot be undone with these tools; a staged removal becomes permanent
once the interface is published.
Use list_pages_for_base to find the pageId if needed.
After deleting, only offer to run publish_interface when the removal was
staged — i.e. the page had its own published version. If it was removed immediately (a
standalone form, or a page with no published version), the deletion already took effect for
end users, so do not suggest publishing.

