 | {
kind: "readOnlyNodeType",
// The read-only node type (e.g. "noOp") present in the request. Read-only nodes can be read via get_automation but never created or modified through this API; edit them in the Airtable UI instead.
providedNodeType: string,
}
 | {
kind: "reservedNodeKey",
// The reserved key the agent attempted to use.
providedKey: string,
// The full set of reserved keys agents must avoid.
reservedKeys: string[],
}
 | {
kind: "duplicateNodeKey",
// The duplicated key. Each node key must be unique within the automation; rename one of the colliding nodes.
providedKey: string,
}
 | {
kind: "nestedRepeatingGroup",
// The repeatingGroup key that was (transitively) nested inside another repeatingGroup.
providedKey: string,
}
 | {
kind: "nodeAfterDecisionGroup",
// The repeatingGroup/conditionalGroup key that was followed by another node. A decision group must be the last node in its sequence.
providedKey: string,
}
 | {
kind: "missingRepeatingGroupItems",
// The repeatingGroup key whose `inputs.items` array source was missing or null.
providedKey: string,
}
 | {
kind: "elseBranchNotLast",
// The conditionalGroup key that had a null-condition (else) branch before its last branch. Only the last branch may have a null condition.
providedKey: string,
}
 | {
kind: "emptyBranchNotNested",
// The conditionalGroup key that had an empty branch while not nested in a repeatingGroup. Empty branches are only allowed when the group is nested in a repeatingGroup.
providedKey: string,
}
 | {
kind: "tooManyActions",
// The maximum number of action nodes allowed in a single automation.
maxNumActions: number,
}
 | {
kind: "maxNestingDepthExceeded",
// The decision-group key whose children would exceed the maximum nesting depth. Flatten the automation so groups nest no deeper than `maxNestingDepth`.
providedKey: string,
// The maximum decision-group nesting depth allowed (top-level nodes are depth 0).
maxNestingDepth: number,
}
 | {
kind: "invalidConditionOperator",
// The operator name the agent supplied that did not resolve. Use an operator name Airtable filters use (e.g. "=", "!=", "contains", "isEmpty", "hasAnyOf") matching the comparison `dataType`.
providedOperator: string,
// The comparison `dataType` ("literal" or "array") the operator was resolved against. "literal" expects scalar operators; "array" expects array operators ("contains"/"doesNotContain"/"isEmpty"/"isNotEmpty").
dataType: string,
}
 | {
kind: "invalidConditionShape",
// Human-readable reason the branch condition was structurally invalid (e.g. a comparison missing its `left` operand).
reason: string,
}
 | {
kind: "outputSchemaNotSupported",
// The action type that does not support outputSchema.
providedNodeType: string,
}
 | {
kind: "secretsNotSupported",
// The action type that does not support secrets.
providedNodeType: string,
}
,
}
>,
// An opaque action ID that can be passed to revert_action to undo the update. Present only when the update succeeds.
actionId?: string, // pattern: /^act[A-Za-z0-9]{14}$/
}>;
```

Updates the name, description, and/or options of a field in an existing Airtable table.
At least one of name, description, or options must be specified.
To get baseId and tableId, use the search_bases and list_tables_for_base tools first.
To get the fieldId, use the list_tables_for_base tool.
Example: update a field's name and description:
{"baseId": "appZfrNIUEip5MazD", "tableId": "tblGlReoTNWfYnXIG", "fieldId": "fldGlRtkBNWfYnPOV", "name": "Updated Name", "description": "Updated description"}
Example: update a formula field's expression:
{"baseId": "appZfrNIUEip5MazD", "tableId": "tblGlReoTNWfYnXIG", "fieldId": "fldGlRtkBNWfYnPOV", "options": {"formula": "{Quantity} * {Price}"}}

```ts
mcp__Airtable__update_field(args: {
// The ID of the base containing the table.
// Must start with "app" and is 17 characters long.
// Example: "appZfrNIUEip5MazD".
// Do not substitute user-facing names for baseId.
// To get baseId, use the search_bases or list_bases tool.
baseId: string, // pattern: /^app[A-Za-z0-9]{14}$/
// The ID of the table containing the field.
// Must start with "tbl" and is 17 characters long.
// Example: "tblGlReoTNWfYnXIG".
// Do not substitute user-facing names for tableId.
// To get tableId, use the list_tables_for_base tool.
tableId: string, // pattern: /^tbl[A-Za-z0-9]{14}$/
// The ID of the field to update.
// Field IDs must start with "fld" and is 17 characters long.
// Example: "fldGlRtkBNWfYnPOV".
// Do not substitute user-facing names for IDs.
// To get fieldId, use the list_tables_for_base tool.
fieldId: string, // pattern: /^fld[A-Za-z0-9]{14}$/
// The new name for the field. Must be unique within the table (case-insensitive).
name?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 255
description?: string, // maxLength: 20000
// Type-specific field options.
options?: {
// The new formula expression (formula fields only). Reference fields by name ({Field Name}) or ID ({fldXXXXXXXXXXXXXX}).
formula?: string, // minLength: 1
},
}): Promise<{
success: boolean,
// The action ID of this field update; pass to revert_action to undo it.
actionId?: string, // pattern: /^act[A-Za-z0-9]{14}$/
}>;
```

Updates records in an Airtable table.
The fields you specify will be updated, and all other fields will be left unchanged.
To get baseId and tableId, consider using the search_bases and list_tables_for_base tools first.
When writing to a linked-record (multipleRecordLinks) field through an interface page, get the
record IDs from search_candidate_linked_records, passing a pageId that exposes
the field for editing — it also applies the field's record-selection filters. It only works
within interfaces; for base-level writes, use record IDs from the linked table.
For singleSelect/multipleSelects fields, provide the option name as a plain string (e.g., "In progress") or array of strings, not the object format returned by list_records_for_table.
By default the response includes only the fields you wrote. To also include fields you did not write (e.g. the primary field or formula results), pass their IDs in fieldIds.
You can update up to 50 records per request. To update more than 50 records, make multiple requests.
Example: update a record's fields:
{"baseId": "appZfrNIUEip5MazD", "tableId": "tblGlReoTNWfYnXIG", "records": [{"id": "recZOTa3BDHxlJNzf", "fields": {"fldGlRtkBNWfYnPOV": "Updated name", "fld8WsrpLHHevsnW8": "Done"}}]}

```ts
mcp__Airtable__update_records_for_table(args: {
// The ID of the base containing the table.
// Must start with "app" and is 17 characters long.
// Example: "appZfrNIUEip5MazD".
// Do not substitute user-facing names for baseId.
// To get baseId, use the search_bases or list_bases tool.
baseId: string, // pattern: /^app[A-Za-z0-9]{14}$/
// The ID of the table to update records in.
// Must start with "tbl" and is 17 characters long.
// Example: "tblGlReoTNWfYnXIG".
// Do not substitute user-facing names for tableId.
// To get tableId, use the list_tables_for_base tool.
tableId: string, // pattern: /^tbl[A-Za-z0-9]{14}$/
// An array of record objects to update. Each record must have a "fields" property
// containing the field values.
// minItems: 1
records: Array<
{
// The ID of the record to update.
// Required when performUpsert is not set.
// Must start with "rec" and is 17 characters long.
// Example: "recZOTa3BDHxlJNzf".
// Do not substitute user-facing names for IDs
// To get recordId, use the list_records_for_table tool or display_records_for_table tools.
id?: string, // pattern: /^rec[A-Za-z0-9]{14}$/
// An object containing field IDs as keys and field values as values.
// Field values should match the field type (e.g., strings for singleLineText fields,
// numbers for numeric fields, arrays of strings for multipleSelects fields).
// For singleSelect fields, use the option name as a plain string (e.g., "Done").
// For multipleSelects fields, use an array of option name strings (e.g., ["Tag1", "Tag2"]).
// For multipleRecordLinks (linked-record) fields, use an array of record IDs from the linked table.
// Field IDs must start with "fld" and is 17 characters long.
// Example: "fldGlRtkBNWfYnPOV".
// Do not substitute user-facing names for IDs.
// To get fieldId, use the list_tables_for_base tool.
fields: { [key: string]: any },
}
>,
// Enables upsert behavior when set.
// When upserting is enabled, the recordId parameter is optional.
// Records that do not include a recordId will use the fields chosen by the fieldIdsToMergeOn parameter to match with existing records.
// - If no matches are found, a new record will be created.
// - If a match is found, that record will be updated.
// - If multiple matches are found, the request will fail.
// Records that include id will ignore fieldIdsToMergeOn and behave as normal updates.
// If no record with the given id exists, the request will fail and will not create a new record
performUpsert?: {
// An array of field IDs that will be used to match records for updates.
// These fields must be unique and must not be computed fields (formulas, lookups, rollups).
// Field IDs must start with "fld" and is 17 characters long.
// Example: "fldGlRtkBNWfYnPOV".
// Do not substitute user-facing names for IDs.
// To get fieldId, use the list_tables_for_base tool.
fieldIdsToMergeOn: string[],
},
// Whether or not to perform best-effort automatic data conversion from string values.
// Defaults to false to preserve data integrity.
typecast?: boolean,
// The IDs of the fields to include in each returned record.
// If omitted, only the fields you wrote (the keys of records[].fields, unioned across all input records) are returned.
// Pass explicit IDs to include fields you did not write (e.g. the primary field or formula/rollup results).
// Field IDs must start with "fld" and is 17 characters long.
// Example: "fldGlRtkBNWfYnPOV".
// Do not substitute user-facing names for IDs.
// To get fieldId, use the list_tables_for_base tool.
fieldIds?: Array<
string // pattern: /^fld[A-Za-z0-9]{14}$/
>,
// Set this only when the user lacks base access (which can be determined by the
// permission listed on list_bases) and is updating records through an
// interface they collaborate on. When provided, the update is authorized against the
// user's collaborator permissions on the given interface instead of base-level
// permissions.
interfaceContext?: {
// The ID of the interface for which the update is being performed.
// Must start with "pbd" and is 17 characters long.
interfaceId: string, // pattern: /^pbd[A-Za-z0-9]{14}$/
},
}): Promise<{
records: Array<

 | {
// The ID of the record.
id: string, // pattern: /^rec[A-Za-z0-9]{14}$/
// The time the record was created.
createdTime: string,
// The cell values of the record by field ID.
cellValuesByFieldId: { [key: string]: any },
}
// Returned when interfaceContext is set and the updated record is no longer readable through that interface, e.g. because the update moved it outside the page filters.
 | {
// The ID of the updated record.
id: string, // pattern: /^rec[A-Za-z0-9]{14}$/
}

>,
hint?: string,
}>;
```

