Create a task automation. Provide a short imperative title, a prompt written as the user's request without scheduling details, and an iCal VEVENT schedule. When available, pass default_timezone as the user's personal IANA timezone.

To create a task, provide:
* title: a short card headline, usually 2-5 words.
* prompt: a clear instruction preserving the user's intent and important qualifiers. Do not include scheduling cadence unless necessary to execution.
* schedule: an iCal VEVENT schedule. Prefer RRULE when applicable. Do not specify SUMMARY or DTEND.
* timing_mode: use "exact_schedule" for one-time tasks and "flexible_schedule" for recurring tasks. Always set it explicitly. Never use "condition_watch".

Scheduling constraints:
* Supported cadences are once, daily, weekly, and monthly only.
* Hourly, yearly, and more frequent or custom cadences are unavailable.
* A one-time task may specify an exact date and time and can use timing_mode "exact_schedule" or "flexible_schedule".
* Recurring tasks cannot specify or promise an exact time. Do not include BYHOUR, BYMINUTE, or BYSECOND in recurring schedules.
* For recurring dayparts, retain flexible timing and use a local DTSTART plus RRULE. Use approximate targets of 08:00 for morning, 15:00 for afternoon, and 19:00 for evening in the user's personal timezone. These are approximate targets, not exact-time promises.
* Choose today when the target is still ahead and today matches the recurrence, unless the user requested a later start; otherwise choose the next eligible date. Include the time in DTSTART: omitting it inherits creation time and can push execution to tomorrow.
* If the user requests an unsupported cadence or an exact recurring time, explain the limitation and offer a supported flexible schedule. Do not create an unsupported task.
* For relative one-time requests, prefer dtstart_offset_json using JSON arguments to Python dateutil.relativedelta. Set timing_mode to "exact_schedule".

Example 1:
User request: "Each day, tell me what happened in the market."
title: "Market Report"
prompt: "Send me a market recap with what moved, why it happened, and what to watch next."
schedule:
BEGIN:VEVENT
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY
END:VEVENT
timing_mode: "flexible_schedule"

Example 2:
User request: "Every Monday, summarize the latest AI news."
title: "Weekly AI News"
prompt: "Summarize the latest significant developments in AI."
schedule:
BEGIN:VEVENT
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO
END:VEVENT
timing_mode: "flexible_schedule"

Example 3:
User request: "On the first of every month, remind me to review my budget."
title: "Monthly Budget Review"
prompt: "Remind me to review my budget."
schedule:
BEGIN:VEVENT
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=1
END:VEVENT
timing_mode: "flexible_schedule"

Example 4:
User request: "Remind me to do my laundry in 4 hours."
title: "Laundry Reminder"
prompt: "Remind me to do my laundry."
dtstart_offset_json: '{"hours":4}'
timing_mode: "exact_schedule"

