Define a new entity type with its field structure. This creates the schema only — to add data records, use create_entities. Always check existing schemas with list_entity_schemas first.

## Row-Level Security (RLS)
Entity schemas can include RLS rules under the 'rls' field to restrict record access based on user identity. RLS rules are defined per operation: create, read, update, delete.

Template variables: {{user.id}}, {{user.email}}, {{user.role}}, {{user.data.<field>}}.

Rule types:
1. user_condition — exact equality check on user attributes (no MongoDB operators). E.g. {"user_condition": {"role": "admin"}}
2. Entity-user field comparison — MongoDB query syntax. Custom fields MUST use "data." prefix (e.g. "data.user_id": "{{user.id}}"). Built-in fields (id, created_by_id, created_date, updated_date) are at root level.

Combine with $and/$or/$in/$nin. Rules must reference user template variables, never static values.

Example: {"rls": {"read": {"created_by_id": "{{user.id}}"}, "update": {"$or": [{"created_by_id": "{{user.id}}"}, {"user_condition": {"role": "admin"}}]}}}

